#: package/analyses/ega.description
msgid "Estimates how many dimensions underlie a set of items, and which items belong to each, by modeling the items as a network of regularized partial correlations and grouping densely connected items with a community detection algorithm. Reports the number of dimensions, item memberships, network loadings and the Total Entropy Fit Index, with a network plot and plain-language interpretation. Use it as the first step in assessing the dimensional structure of a scale, before checking its stability with Bootstrap EGA."
msgstr ""

#: ega/options.description.main
msgid "Estimates the number of dimensions underlying a set of items, and which items belong to each dimension, with Exploratory Graph Analysis (EGAnet), paired with network loadings, entropy fit and plain-language interpretation."
msgstr ""

